  "historical_output_text": " Surething\n\nCertainly![Your Garden's Path Forward]\n\n1-2. Start your garden preparation at least 8 hours or so prior. This helps in making your soil ready with time. If it is too early and your ground's surface still looks too sogged from last evening, it is fine - it means there’s a little time for natural moisture absorption. Soak a few garden forks deep down to break and flake clump soils and roots into small, crumbed bits that make good, rich hum. The more air gets incorporated, leading into better aeration.\n\nThis step prepares you and the land by breaking down compact soil to encourage root movement. A well-cleared ground will support a robust and expansive growth.\n\n4a and onward - Lay your soil to one or another. You want your garden's surface flat. Use the trow",
